    <a href="#maincontent" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>

    <header>
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
            <p>Everything you ever wanted to know about cats.</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="example">
                <h2>
                    <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="disclosure-trigger">
                        Why do cats purr?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div class="details">
                    <p>Cats purr for many reasons, including contentment, self-soothing when they are stressed or in pain, and even as a way to communicate with their kittens or humans. The frequency of a cat's purr has also been shown to help with bone and tissue healing.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="example">
                <h2>
                    <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="disclosure-trigger">
                        Why do cats like boxes?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div class="details">
                    <p>Boxes provide cats with a sense of security and safety. In the wild, cats are both predators and prey, so having a confined space where they can't be snuck up on from behind or the side is very comforting. It also helps them stay warm, as corrugated cardboard is a great insulator.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="example">
                <h2>
                    <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="disclosure-trigger">
                        Why do cats have whiskers?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div class="details">
                    <p>Whiskers are highly sensitive tactile organs. They help cats navigate in the dark, detect changes in air currents (which can signal nearby prey), and determine if they can fit through tight spaces. A cat's whiskers are generally as wide as their body.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="example">
                <h2>
                    <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="disclosure-trigger">
                        How many hours a day do cats sleep?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div class="details">
                    <p>On average, cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Some cats can even sleep up to 20 hours in a 24-hour period. This is an evolutionary trait from their ancestors who needed to conserve energy for intense bursts of hunting.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="example">
                <h2>
                    <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="disclosure-trigger">
                        Why do cats "knead" or make biscuits?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div class="details">
                    <p>Kneading is a behavior cats carry over from kittenhood. Nursing kittens knead their mothers to stimulate milk flow. As adults, they continue this behavior when they feel happy, comfortable, and safe, often on soft surfaces like blankets or their favorite humans.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <div class="container">
            <p>&copy; 2026 Feline Facts Hub. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
            const triggers = document.querySelectorAll('.disclosure-trigger');

            triggers.forEach(trigger => {
                const panel = trigger.closest('h2').nextElementSibling;

                // Initialize state: collapsed by default
                trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                panel.hidden = true;

                trigger.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    const isExpanded = trigger.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
                    trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !isExpanded);
                    panel.hidden = isExpanded;
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
